# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so everything that should
# stay out of the build archive has to be repeated here.
#
# It exists as a local/CI fallback for google-services.json, which is restored from a
# secret rather than committed. Current EAS builds also sync the file through the
# GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON file environment variable; that is the authoritative remote-worker
# path. The explicit `!` rule below still includes the generated local file when supported.
#
# google-services.json is a client-side Firebase config that already ships inside the APK,
# so uploading it to the EAS builder is safe.
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
*.jks
*.keystore
ios/
android/

# Include the Firebase client config generated by CI even though .gitignore excludes it.
# Keep this rule last so it overrides every earlier ignore rule.
!google-services.json
